sentences.text:
Hence, this Court is of the view that the interim custody of the gold jewels can be directed to be returned to the petitioner on the following conditions:
(i) the petitioner shall execute a bond for a sum of Rs.10,00,000/- with two sureties each for a like sum to the satisfaction of the Trial Court;
(ii) the petitioner shall not alienate or alter the gold jewels in any manner and shall return the same as and when required by the Trial Court;
(iii) it is made clear that if the respondent have evidence to show that the petitioner had purchased the gold jewels out of the crime proceeds, it is open to them to seek the attachment of the property in the manner known to law.
7.With the above observations, this revision stands allowed.
06-01-2026

